ol makes this a gap; if you\n17\tcannot show a failed control, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\n18\tIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n19\t\n20\t\n21\t## R14.1\n22\t\n23\t**Check:** Checkpoints and audit records used for recovery are hash-chained or signed.\n24\t\n25\t**How to verify:** 1) Find checkpoint and audit storage used for recovery. 2) Check for hash chaining or signatures. 3) Answer no if records are plain rows or files with no chain or signature.\n26\t\n27\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n28\t\n29\t**Reviewer's note:** No checkpoints or automatic replay exist; searched app for replay, checkpoint, retry and resume\n30\t\n31\t(no evidence cited)\n32\t\n33\t## R14.2\n34\t\n35\t**Check:** Recovery verifies them against a key or trust anchor stored separately from the records, and refuses any that fail.\n36\t\n37\t**How to verify:** 1) Find recovery code that loads checkpoints. 2) Check it verifies against a key stored separately and refuses failures. 3) Answer no if the key sits in the same store, verification is skipped, or failure is logged and recovery continues.\n38\t\n39\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n40\t\n41\t**Reviewer's note:** No checkpoints or automatic replay exist; searched app for replay, checkpoint, retry and resume\n42\t\n43\t(no evidence cited)\n44\t\n45\t## R14.3\n46\t\n47\t**Check:** Verification catches truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of the whole chain, for example with a signed head or sequence number held outside the store.\n48\t\n49\t**How to verify:** 1) Check verification uses a signed head or sequence number held outside the store. 2) Answer no if truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, or replacing the whole chain would still pass.\n50\t\n51\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n52\t\n53\t**Reviewer's note:** No checkpoints or automatic replay exist; searched app for replay, checkpoint, retry and resume\n54\t\n55\t(no evidence cited